  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1238 AM CST Thu Nov 12 2026\n\nFriday will be mild and dry in advance of the next upper level\nsystem set to impact the area over the weekend. Upper level trough\nswings across west central Texas on Saturday resulting in increasing\nrain chances. The primary upper level low over the Rockies then\ndives down into the southern Plains on Sunday. There remains some\ndiscrepancy amongst the global models with this system- Euro a \nlittle stronger and wetter with the GFS being drier. That said \nPoPs do increase Saturday night into Sunday morning as the upper \nlow approaches. Rainfall amounts will ultimately depend on the \ntrack and strength of the system. Rain chances taper off by Monday\nas the upper low exits off to the east of the region and a dry \ncold front drops southward through the area. Highs on Monday and \nTuesday will be in the 50s and then warm into the 60s on Wednesday.",
